WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.609
Hey guys, Pete here. Today I'm back with
another Dark season 3 video. I've been

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:10.559
rewatching the final season to add to my
notes, and today I have 33 details that

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:13.799
you might have missed.
I think 33 is the right number, but it's

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:17.730
a big number, so I want to jump right in.
Before we get started though I've got to

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.840
state the obvious, that this video will
contain spoilers if you haven't finished

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.340
watching dark season 3 yet. now we can
get started. Number 1 is that

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:30.660
everything's mirrored in alt Martha's
world. I had a lot of comments asking

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.670
about why the scratch on Martha's cheek
moved from side to side in different

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:40.410
scenes. the answer is that the creators
use this as a mark to indicate which

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.700
world we're in. it's not just that either
everything is mirrored including the

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.500
interiors of the homes, and the exterior
of places like the cave. this leads me

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.399
to believe that they essentially flipped
the shots after filming them, and what's

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:57.930
crazy about that is that they would have
to dress the sets in reverse. think about

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:01.500
this shot with Magnus and Martha and how
all the print on the stuff in the

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.210
background and his tattoos would have to
be reversed to achieve the effect. in the

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.110
origin world things like Martha's scratch
and the part in Jonas' hair match

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:13.890
Adam's world. and since we're on the
subject of the origin world the next two

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:18.210
items on the list pertain to that. number
two is that there's no power plant in

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:22.020
the origin world. in this shot we can see
that the smokestacks are noticeably

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.130
missing. it makes sense that if the
Unknown doesn't exist in the origin

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:30.299
world and therefore never forces through
the paperwork, that the coal lobby would

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:34.560
be able to block the power plant from
being built. number three is that they

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.060
use a different aspect ratio when we
visit that world to set it apart. we see

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:42.930
that the black bars above and below
the image are slightly larger and the

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:46.829
color grading seems brighter. since they
already used a mirror effect for Adam

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:51.119
and Eva's worlds they needed a different
visual clue to help mark where we were.

00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:55.409
there are a few subtle differences
thrown in like the location of the bus

00:01:55.409 --> 00:01:59.280
stop and the different door on the
entrance to the bunker as well. number

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.060
four speaking of things that look the
same but different, Dark has always done

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.810
a terrific job of casting actors who
resemble each other to portray

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.860
characters showing up at different ages
through the story. season 3 is no

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.410
exception and this time they even cast
some

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:18.060
real-life father and sons. for the adult
Unknown and the older version they cast

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:23.220
Jacob and Hans Diehl who clearly have a
family resemblance. the one that really

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:27.180
blew me away though was the character
they cast to portray a teenage Peter

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:32.610
Doppler. for this they cast Stephan Kampwirth's real-life son Pablo Striebek for

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.660
the part. I love the way they set up this
scene and I literally yelled out, "Its Peter!"

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:41.130
when he turned to the camera.
number five is about another great scene

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:45.180
in Episode two when Elizabeth and
Charlotte are together in the cave.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.590
Charlotte gets up to walk away and as
she goes Elizabeth tells her everything

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:54.300
will be okay. this pair who are each
other's mother then come together to

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:57.980
comfort each other which is a callback
to season 1 when they did the same thing.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:02.340
number 6 is also about Charlotte and
Elisabeth because I've had a lot of

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:06.150
questions related to these two.
first it was assumed that Claudia was

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.840
the one who stole baby Charlotte away
from Noah and Elisabeth. we learned in

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:15.150
episode 7 that Adam actually sent older
Charlotte and older Elisabeth to take

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.930
her to Tannhaus. in his conversation
with teenager Charlotte we learned a

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:22.890
couple more things as well. he tells her
about the strange women who showed up at

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:27.300
his door with her. he tells her on that
same day his son and his wife died in a

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.750
car crash with his granddaughter, and
that the baby's body was never found.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:35.160
because of that he was able to pass off
Charlotte who was brought to him from

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:38.640
the future as his real granddaughter. so
in the scene when he tells her about

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.600
that she's learning for the first time
that they aren't related by blood and

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:47.100
that he has no idea who her real parents
are. the story of the Doppler family keeps

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:52.160
getting crazier, but the couple from
number 7 actually managed to outdo them.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.030
that is of course Martha and Jonas who
we learned are the center of the family

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:01.320
tree knot that is Winden. Jonas and alt
Martha have a child together and things

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:05.790
get really interesting from there. their
son who appears as a trio of characters

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:10.470
at three different ages doesn't have a
name so he's referred to as the Unknown.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:15.660
after he's born he impregnates both
Agnes Nielsen's in both worlds which

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:20.790
connects everyone beyond that back to
Jonas and Martha. the male line goes Jonas &gt;

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:27.060
Unknown &gt; Tronte &gt; Ulrich &gt; Mikkel &gt; Jonas. so if
you're keeping track that makes

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:30.450
Jonas his own
great-great-great-grandfather.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:34.440
another interesting detail here is the
couple is really the beginning and the

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.639
end of things. they start the knot and
then later undo it when they travel to

00:04:38.639 --> 00:04:43.180
the origin world where none of their
descendants exist. speaking of mr. Kahnwald

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.639
number eight is this shot of him
dying in Eva's world. the way he's laying

00:04:47.639 --> 00:04:51.780
on the ground makes the family tree look
like angel wings and that's interesting

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:56.790
since Tannhaus' daughter-in-law Sonja
mentions angels after Jonas and Martha

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:00.570
stopped them from getting into the car
crash. he's dying on the floor of Eva's

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:05.760
lair and number nine is the name of her
group. Adam's world has Sic Mundus and

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:10.800
Eva's has Erit Lux which translates to
there will be light. we see this on the

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:15.780
metal door to the passage in her world.
number ten is Erit Lux's symbol which

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:19.710
is two snakes with wings. this is called
a caduceus symbol and what you might

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:24.060
have missed is that Magnus has a tattoo
of this above his sternum. for number

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.990
eleven will stay on Eva and her lair. you
might have missed that her family tree

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:32.370
is actually wrong. it has Tronte listed
as Regina's father which was the popular

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:36.780
theory heading in the season. three it
turned out that Claudia and Bernd Doppler

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:40.680
were Regina's parents and what's
interesting about this is that Claudia

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:44.970
was probably deceiving Eva since she's
likely the only person who knew the

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:50.250
truth. number twelve is also related to
parentage at the end of episode six when

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:54.810
Eva is sending her travelers back to
preserve the loop she tells Egon to

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:59.190
create his past to preserve the family
tree. a lot of people have been asking

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:03.510
about this so this is my understanding.
in Eva's world Hannah is married to

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:08.160
Ulrich and pregnant with his child at
the time of the apocalypse. just before

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:12.870
the older Egon arrives she suffers a
miscarriage. we know they are still Silja's

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:16.740
parents in both worlds but her path
is different since she hasn't traveled

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:21.360
to the 1950s. this leads me to believe
that Egon will take her there to save

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.320
her from the apocalypse and that will
put her in place to meet the younger

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:30.510
Egon and start their affair. on the
subject of Silja number 13 is the look

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:34.680
on Bartosz's face when he hears that
she wants to name their son Hanno.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:38.760
remember Noah
aka Hanno Tauber is the one who brought

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:42.840
Bartosz into this mess in
first place. so at this moment he would

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:46.949
be realizing that he was meeting with
his own son. what makes us even more

00:06:46.949 --> 00:06:51.419
insane is that we know that Noah kills
his own father in the opening of season

00:06:51.419 --> 00:06:55.350
two. number fourteen is another Silja
one and it's something I didn't notice

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:59.520
myself. I got this one from Kim Renfro's
great "things you might have missed

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:03.570
article" on The Insider website. Kim is
one of my favorite writers because she

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:07.169
always digs deep, and you can tell she's
a fan. I will put a link to her

00:07:07.169 --> 00:07:11.130
article in this video's description
because she includes a lot of stuff from

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:15.570
the first and second season. anyway Kim
pointed out that Silja is wearing the

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:19.860
same clothes she had Martha take off
in the future when she arrives back in

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:25.650
1890 to get together with Bartosz. number
15 deals with that same time period. one

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:30.449
of the biggest questions about Jonas's
story was how he transformed into the

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:35.310
stranger and then later Adam. what a
revelation it is to find out just how

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:39.360
lame that process actually was for him.
we see that he's stuck in post

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:44.370
apocalyptic Winden after surviving the
actual apocalypse. unable to go anywhere

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:49.470
because Eva is making Claudia stall her
progress on stabilizing the god particle.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:53.880
then he goes to do the things we saw him
do in the first two seasons only to get

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:58.380
stuck in 1888 working to build the god
particle twin. what struck me the most

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:02.280
about this was that we had been
wondering how he got his trademark

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:06.810
scarring. my takeaway after season 3 is
that this is a combination of injuries

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:10.590
we see him get burnt at one point and
that makes me believe that instead of

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:14.940
being scarred from time traveling
extensively it's actually more of a

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:19.860
death from a thousand paper cuts kind of
situation. number 16 is one that goes

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:24.840
back even before 1888. we learn about the
origin of the golden watch. several

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:29.820
people asked why'd the blind man, who
turns out to be Gustav Tannhaus, had the

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:33.930
watch in the scene where he's killed by
the Unknown? the answer is that the watch

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:38.130
was passed down from his father,
Heinrich Tannhaus, who originally bought

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:42.060
it for his wife who was named Charlotte.
she died and this led to the formation

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:46.920
of Sic Mundus because Heinrich wanted to
learn about time travel to try to go

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:50.579
back and save her life. the name
Charlotte and the idea of time

00:08:50.579 --> 00:08:54.330
travelling to save a departed loved
one will continue on in the

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:58.769
Tannhaus family throughout the
generations. number 17 is another one

00:08:58.769 --> 00:09:02.370
that I got from Kim's article and it's
about Magnus. when he's in front of the

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:06.870
cave in the 2019 timeline he says
something to the effect of about a

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:11.370
hundred years, just after the war they
did experiments in the caves. this is

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:15.839
interesting because that would be around
the time where Erit Lux would probably

00:09:15.839 --> 00:09:19.560
